        "prose": "Ashai dismissed the last constellation of practice light. Blue motes clung to the air for a breath before winking out. Goaden, waiting near the boundary line, gave one slow nod. “Cleaner.” She raised an eyebrow. “Was that praise?” “Don’t get used to it.” Greah immediately announced that she had witnessed everything."
