        "prose": "The carriage was half empty. Goaden took the window seat and immediately looked nowhere near the window. Ashai sat opposite, watching wards shimmer faintly along the carriage seams whenever the train crossed solid architecture. Neither spoke until the city returned to ordinary shape."
