        "prose": "A ward line travelled the length of the carriage in a soft blue pulse. Conversation dipped as passengers noticed it, then resumed. Ashai followed the light until it disappeared beneath the next door. Goaden glanced towards the ceiling. Nothing else happened, which was the point of good wards."
