        "prose": "Truth's shifting tattoos caught the light every time he moved. Balthazar read one clause through Anarchy's eyes and surfaced in a dark green flicker. “Your institution's lawyers are parasites.” Goaden looked at the paper. “High praise from a demon.” Nobody called it nostalgia."
