        "prose": "The common room clock had slipped well past sensible hours before anyone noticed. Ashai paused in the doorway rather than interrupt. Goaden noticed her reflection in the piano lid. “Couldn’t sleep?” “Could ask you the same.” He moved one hand off the keys. “You could.” Morning remained far enough away to ignore."
